It includes work derived from the following Apache-2.0 licensed projects:

1. "board" layout from herdr-layout-examples
   https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-layout-examples (commit 0ec9676, 2026-11-02)
   Files derived: layouts/herdboard.json, mods/herdboard/
   Changes: renamed; theme colors instead of a fixed palette; one-line header with a
   space strip, filter, search, language switch (pt-BR / English) and menu; Herdr's
   sidebar folded on the left; cards show the task title, real elapsed time and a
   "stuck?" hint; blocked cards show the agent's question (read with `hc read`) with
   answer and peek actions; hover actions (peek, pin, put away); compact, foldable
   Idle column; workspace rail with tabs, new tab, close tab and expand; responsive
   layout and height that follows the columns.

2. "picker" and "new-menu" mods shipped with Herdr (herdr-app 0.1.13)
   https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr
   Files derived: mods/herdboard-picker/, mods/herdboard-new-menu/
   Changes: renamed; texts follow Herdboard's language (pt-BR / English); the new-tab
   menu lets you pick the folder a tab starts in (default: the active tab's live
   folder) and passes it to tab.new, and with the machine to space.new.
